; MOON.EXE: the game of Battle Isle's second data disk (Borland C++, large
; model, 4585 relocations): the same engine as BATTLE.EXE, presumably,
; its modules sized and laid out somewhat otherwise; the hints below the
; marker are BATTLE.hints' carried over by doskit/tools/xfer.py.
; Hints for doskit/tools/disasm.py; numbers are hex.

exe MOON/MOON.EXE

; the segments, from the relocations and the header (SS:SP = 3021:0080;
; the file ends with the stack); DS holds DGROUP (DATA, 2EAE: a run
; loaded the program at 0076 and had DS = 2F24 at CODE:0116). The code
; segments T.... begin where the one before ends (start=, the lowest
; offset below 10h a far CALL/JMP enters each by; 0 where none does);
; F.... far data as in BATTLE.EXE (the class a guess)
segment CODE  0000 CODE
segment T039B 039B CODE start=7 prefix=T039B_
segment T03EB 03EB CODE start=6 prefix=T03EB_
segment T070B 070B CODE start=A prefix=T070B_
segment T0BDE 0BDE CODE start=E prefix=T0BDE_
segment T0C0E 0C0E CODE start=C prefix=T0C0E_
segment T0D67 0D67 CODE start=3 prefix=T0D67_
segment T0DA1 0DA1 CODE start=1 prefix=T0DA1_
segment T0F3E 0F3E CODE start=E prefix=T0F3E_
