; The mouse (INT 33h), read in full; runs of ISLE's first map with the
; runner's -mouse (docs/HANDOFF.md) showed the directions, the centring,
; fire with a direction, and the two keys. The mouse is a joystick for one
; player: how far the driver's position is from 160, 100 gives the
; directions, the left button is fire.
; mouse_start (mode, record, shown): 1 when the mouse is on already; INT
; 33h AX=0, -1 unless it answers FFFFh; the buttons' number to DATA:0438,
; mouse_on FFFFh, the three arguments kept (mouse_by_timer, mouse_record,
; mouse_shown: every call passes 0, a player's events record, 0), the
; driver's sensitivity kept for mouse_stop (AX=1Bh; DATA:0446..044A), then
; mouse_read.
; mouse_read: -1 when the mouse is off; INT 33h AX=3: mouse_x and mouse_y,
; and for each button FFFFh when down (mouse_left, DATA:043C the middle,
; mouse_right). With mouse_shown and the place another than the last
; (DATA:041E, 0420) it saves three VGA registers, exchanges the pages
; twice with nothing between (a pointer drawn there once, presumably),
; sets DATA:0412 and keeps the place. timer_keys calls it every tick when
; mouse_by_timer is 1, mouse_input when it is 0.
; mouse_stop: -1 when off; with DATA:0412 what the pointer covered is put
; back (T24D3:0000 with DATA:0364 and pointer_store, on the page shown);
; the sensitivity given back (AX=1Ah), mouse_on and DATA:0412 0.
; mouse_rates (x, y, x held, y held, double, threshold, threshold held):
; -1 when off; the mickeys a pixel set (AX=0Fh) and kept (DATA:0422, 0424),
; the double-speed threshold (AX=13h; 0FA0h in every call), the rates
; while the left button is held (DATA:0426, 0428), the two thresholds
; (DATA:042A, 042C) and mouse_threshold the first. The callers pass one
; number four times, 32h, 0Ah or 3 by mouse_speed (0, 1, 2; the menu's
; SLOW, MEDIUM and a third), and 28h for both thresholds.
; mouse_input (SI the five bytes left, right, up, down, fire of the
; pass): called by the players' input (T2354:02A4) for the player whose
; events record is mouse_record. The left button going down sets the held
; rates and threshold (DATA:0414 FFFFh), going up the others and centres;
; if the right button is down then, DATA:044C counts ten passes of which
; the eight after the first give no direction (read, not run). Both buttons down:
; nothing. Else mouse_x - 160 at or above mouse_threshold is right, at or
; below its negative left, mouse_y - 100 likewise down and up, each with
; mouse_centre; the left button down is fire.
; mouse_centre: with neither button down the driver's place is set back
; to 160, 100 (AX=4), so a direction lasts until the next reading.
; The callers: T0708 at the start (mouse_stop, mouse_start for player 0,
; mouse_rates 0Ah) and at the end (mouse_stop); the menu (after T1090:0C1D's
; flip_page mouse_rates by mouse_speed each pass; before T1090:0E97
; mouse_stop and mouse_start for the player mouse_player says, above 0
; player 1); the
; map's loop: the key at the key set's +12h (scancode 41h, F7, in a run's
; memory) switches the mouse off (message 38h) or on for mouse_player's
; player (37h), the key at +13h (42h, F8) takes the next mouse_speed
; while it is on (messages 39h, 3Ah, 3Bh), both only while game_flags2
; has no 200h.
name T2757:0004 mouse_start
name T2711:0004 mouse_read
name T2750:0008 mouse_stop
name T275E:0000 mouse_rates
name T249A:0397 mouse_input
name T249A:04A0 mouse_centre
